## Installation

{% install primitive="debug" /%}

## Example

Add it once, at the end of `<body>`, in the pages you develop on. It audits the whole page and logs its findings to the console. On a hostname it doesn't list, it removes itself and logs one warning saying so (`data-debug-warnings="false"` silences that), so the tag can stay in a shared template.

```html
<ui-debug data-debug-domains="localhost, staging.example.com"></ui-debug>
```

When you upgrade, the audit also reports `data-ui` tokens the kit has retired and names each replacement. A leftover `data-ui="sr-only"` matches no rule, so without it the hidden text just appears on the page.

